From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:24:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/vpd: A missing VPD region is not a warning

init_vpd_rdevs() looks for both RO_VPD and RW_VPD and prints a warning
for the one the FMAP does not have. A board may have only one of them:
the ThinkCentre M920x and the W541 have only RO_VPD, and get
"init_vpd_rdev: No RW_VPD FMAP section." as a warning at every boot.
Print it as information.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/drivers/vpd/vpd.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/vpd/vpd.c b/src/drivers/vpd/vpd.c
index 56b09263c3..7d809c3ce8 100644
--- a/src/drivers/vpd/vpd.c
+++ b/src/drivers/vpd/vpd.c
@@ -52,7 +52,8 @@ static void init_vpd_rdev(const char *fmap_name, struct region_device *rdev)
 	int32_t size;
 
 	if (fmap_locate_area_as_rdev(fmap_name, rdev)) {
-		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "%s: No %s FMAP section.\n", __func__,
+		/* Not an error: a board may have only one of RO_VPD and RW_VPD */
+		printk(BIOS_INFO, "%s: No %s FMAP section.\n", __func__,
 			fmap_name);
 		goto fail;
 	}
